@prefix : <https://w3id.org/ddta/process#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@base <https://w3id.org/ddta/process> .

<https://w3id.org/ddta/process>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "DDTA Process Ontology (experimental bootstrap)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Experimental DDTA module for domain-independent process composition and control flow. This bootstrap declares no process classes or properties. Terms are introduced individually after a documented use case, semantic review and tests. It reuses the identities of DDTA Core without redefining them."@en .

# ============================================================================
# STATUS: EXPERIMENTAL_NON_CANONICAL / BOOTSTRAP ONLY
# ============================================================================
# Ontology IRI:     https://w3id.org/ddta/process
# Term namespace:   https://w3id.org/ddta/process#
# Source file:      projects/ddta-semantic-workspace/ontology/process.ttl
#
# The w3id.org/ddta path has NOT been registered/verified for public resolution.
# No owl:imports yet: ontology resolution/loading must be tested locally before
# committing to import semantics. Core remains the source of truth for
# ddta:Function, ddta:Process, ddta:hasInput, ddta:hasOutput, ddta:hasPart,
# ddta:realizesFunction and all other existing generic terms.
#
# The lines below are deliberately COMMENTS, NOT RDF/OWL declarations.
# There is no implementation of these constructs in this bootstrap.
# A candidate's name does not authorize its use in project Turtle documents.
#
# ============================================================================
# PROCESS DESIGN INVARIANTS (TO BE TESTED AS TERMS ARE ADDED)
# ============================================================================
# 1. Function = stable capability; Process = structured pattern of activities;
#    ProcessStep (candidate) = an occurrence/role of an activity within a
#    particular process. Do not confuse a step with the function it uses.
# 2. Planned process structure != actual process execution or its outcome.
# 3. Shared output/input does NOT, by itself, entail execution order.
# 4. Composition (ddta:hasPart) does NOT, by itself, entail order or control.
# 5. A documentation Decision (DDTA authoring construct) is NOT a runtime branch.
# 6. A Condition describes an applicability rule; its truth in a specific run
#    requires explicit contextual facts/evaluation, not missing RDF triples.
# 7. No domain-specific AI, deployment or STRIDE concepts belong here.
# 8. RDF semantics, SPARQL selection and Mermaid notation remain separate.
#
# ============================================================================
# CANDIDATE IMPLEMENTATION BACKLOG -- NOT YET APPROVED
# ============================================================================
#
# [CANDIDATE A] Step identity and membership
#   Possible concept: ProcessStep, link to ddta:Process.
#   Questions: Is a Step a kind of ddta:Process or a role within one?
#              Can the same Function occur in several steps/processes?
#              How should steps reference a ddta:Function without violating
#              the existing domain of ddta:realizesFunction?
#   Existing references for comparison: P-Plan Step/Plan, OWL-S processes.
#   First possible test case: DEC-C6-01 setup stages.
#
# [CANDIDATE B] Precedence / control-flow transitions
#   Possible designs: binary 'precedes' relation OR a first-class transition
#   with source and destination steps. Do not select prematurely.
#   Distinguish immediate ordering, transitive precedence, sequencing,
#   and possible non-adjacent dependencies.
#   Existing references: P-Plan isPreceededBy, BPMN sequence flows, OWL-S.
#   First possible test case: six ordered stages in DEC-C6-01.
#
# [CANDIDATE C] Branches and guards
#   Possible concepts: Condition, Branch, conditional transition/guard.
#   Distinguish event 'image received' from condition 'image available'.
#   Consider mutually exclusive vs inclusive branch and default branch.
#   First possible test case: image-present and image-absent triage paths
#   at Decision/FR level, NOT as a new MR-level architectural fact.
#
# [DEFERRED] Concurrency, parallelism, fork/join and synchronization
#   Do not confuse concurrency (overlap/interleaving possible) with actual
#   simultaneous execution. Specify start/completion semantics when needed.
#
# [DEFERRED] Loop, retry, timeout, failure and compensation paths
#   Define only for a documented process that requires them.
#
# [DEFERRED] Execution/provenance
#   Planned steps, executed activities, observations and outcomes are distinct.
#   Compare PROV-O / P-Plan before introducing execution-specific vocabulary.
#
# [DEFERRED] Lifecycle/event/time context
#   A relation may be qualified by time interval, lifecycle phase or events;
#   these differ from runtime guards on a process branch.
#   Coordinate with a potential ddta-lifecycle module and OWL-Time/PROV-O;
#   do not duplicate event identities or make 'valid from/to' part of every
#   process assertion by default.
#
# ============================================================================
# INCREMENTAL ADOPTION RULE
# ============================================================================
# For EVERY new concept/property, in a separate reviewed change:
#   1. Identify one source-supported Decision/FR example and semantic gap.
#   2. State exact meaning, intended scope, domain/range and non-inferences.
#   3. Compare reuse/alignment with P-Plan, OWL-S, BPMN and (if relevant)
#      PROV-O / OWL-Time. Palantir is a conceptual reference, not a source
#      of RDF/OWL axioms to copy.
#   4. Add minimal Turtle vocabulary + positive/negative example + tests.
#   5. Verify RDF parse and intended SPARQL results; use SHACL if needed.
#   6. Only then adapt visualization YAML and generate/check Mermaid.
#   7. Reassess integration with Core without editing Core automatically.
#
# First experimental target when needed: DEC-C6-01 (ordered setup process).
# Later: conditional branches from a documented triage Decision/FR.
